another charge today in goma in north  kivu province  dozens of congolese protesters are  demanding the un peacekeeping mission  called monusco leave the country  the military and police have been called  in to help contain the situation  un personnel are being relocated  the trouble began on monday after a  logistics base was attacked people threw  stones looted office equipment and other  material  this is what was left after it was  ransacked  other un bases have also been targeted  we've been watching the un mission since  the start they have the logistical  capacity they need what are they doing  with that this is why we need to kick  them out  the relationship between some congolese  and the un has been tense at best  the protesters say the u.n has failed to  protect them from frequent attacks  the un peacekeeping mission in  democratic republic of congo has heard a  presence here for more than 20 years  despite this more than a hundred rebel  groups in the east control the versed  region that is rich in minerals  i came to protest against monuca it has  been years since the mission came to  congo many congolese have been killed in  the east  people in goma are fleeing again to  safer areas until the situation gets  better many congolese say they are tired  they want peace and if the u.n cannot  provide stability then its forces need  to leave  catherine soy al jazeera
 

